4. Challenge Track Layout & Milestones


🚩 Milestone 1: The Application Gate Bypass (q1.a / ace.b)

• Vulnerability Profile: The method q1.a within PcPump.Data.dll reads a license-state accessor property (ace.b()) during the instantiation of the manufacturer catalog loader sequence. If this runtime reference resolves to null, a tracking blocker (System.NullReferenceException) triggers immediately, halting database file read operations.
• Tactical Focus: Bypassing key management controls by simulating or forcing a valid security state structure. Participants must trace the assembly execution map using the mandatory REA platform coupled with Ghidra or ILSpy to verify how the application-managed security context is built.
• Verification Token: Capture the runtime memory residue or generate a working C# simulation harness (EngineProbe) demonstrating a stable execution thread through the initialization chain without raising a NullReferenceException.

🚩 Milestone 2: Cryptographic Engine Analysis (FUN_180038c00)

• Vulnerability Profile: Native export analysis of sqlite.interop.dll indicates that the database layer uses the Windows CryptoAPI subsystem rather than simple plaintext passphrases. The internal routine FUN_180038c00 manages duplicate handle functions (CryptDuplicateKey, HCRYPTKEY), meaning the engine requires an active cryptographic context handle to transparently decrypt database tables.
• Tactical Focus: Analyzing the parameters of native functions and determining how symmetric keys are mirrored or managed within the engine context to allow a clean extraction of the database rows.

5. Staging Environment & Compatibility Bounds

• Host Environment: Linux x64 staging hosts utilizing Wine 11.0.0.0 or native Windows runtimes.
• Runtime Dependency: Official Microsoft .NET 8.0 Runtime bundles.
• Analysis Note (Wine Compatibility Defect): Under specific non-Windows runtime layers, native algorithmic providers like BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider("SP800_108_CTR_HMAC") may return initialization failures (0xC0000002 / STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED). This is documented as a platform compatibility variance, not an application code vulnerability. Defect remediation analysis must focus strictly on the application layer components.
